WEBVTT

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:39.710
Éclair and Lumiere?

00:01:39.710 --> 00:01:42.720
Expelled as ES members!?

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:52.060
To Control: This is 2056454, GOTT Destroyer Priamus and LSU Canopus.

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:57.730
On emergency. We want to go runway linear shaft at once.

00:01:57.730 --> 00:02:04.410
Okay, this is Control. Please go runway approach, Priamus and Canopus.

00:02:04.410 --> 00:02:06.740
It's terrible, what's happened, isn't it?

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:10.740
I'm afraid that all we can do is reason it out with them, unfortunately...

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:13.180
That is our job.

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:17.080
You've got a son, don't you?

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:20.420
Yes. He'll be five years old next month.

00:02:20.420 --> 00:02:23.960
Start teaching him now, that no matter what happens,

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:27.430
he is not to take a job with GOTT.

00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:30.430
I'll do that. That is...

00:02:30.430 --> 00:02:33.920
...assuming I make it back home alive.

00:02:34.370 --> 00:02:38.040
Enter warp two minutes and fifteen seconds after we leave the shaft!

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:39.130
Roger.

00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:43.380
Their registrations stricken...

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:47.640
In other words... they're being purged.

00:02:54.050 --> 00:02:58.060
We'll be entering the Zero star system in five minutes and 24 seconds.

00:02:58.060 --> 00:03:01.630
If we're lucky, we'll be able to elude investigation from the head office,

00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:03.860
and may even be able to escape to a colony somewhere.

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:09.740
The closest one is LAV-78. It looks like we'll be okay here.

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:13.570
It has an emigration rate of 87°% . Politically moderate.

00:03:13.570 --> 00:03:17.750
Comparatively easy to get permission to dock.

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:20.410
It's as if we were some kind of fugitives!

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:22.420
There's nothing that can be done about that.

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:25.320
That is, in fact, what we are, after all.

00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:32.030
<i>Our registrations... stricken...</i>

00:03:32.030 --> 00:03:34.660
This is an official notice

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:37.030
from the head office of the government of the Global Union.

00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:40.370
There is nothing else I can do but order you...

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:42.200
Is something the matter?

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:49.040
Look, you! The Chief handed down the orders to purge us unchallenged!

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:50.710
What about it?

00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:53.410
I mean that the relationship of trust between superior and subordinate

00:03:53.410 --> 00:03:56.720
has collapsed. Do you understand?

00:03:56.720 --> 00:04:01.390
Life is long. Many things happen. Particularly...

00:04:01.390 --> 00:04:04.320
...for someone with long lifetimes, like you two have.

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:10.550
It's not like... we live long because we want to!

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:14.070
For some reason, I can't taste this.

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:18.410
You're too concerned about those two. That's probably why.

00:04:18.410 --> 00:04:19.930
'Dledum!

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:23.300
Pardon me, Sister...

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:29.080
"Man is avarice; therefore is he man."

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:32.020
Don't you think that is an interesting proverb?

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:35.360
Everyone dreams of becoming immortally young.

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:38.730
However, once they obtain it, they don't know what to do with it,

00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:41.700
and say they don't want it.

00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:43.230
It's always like that.

00:04:43.230 --> 00:04:45.670
Everyone finds the grass to be greener on the other side,

00:04:45.670 --> 00:04:48.370
while they think of themselves as a third party.

00:04:48.370 --> 00:04:52.540
I am an auditor, so it's my job to do so.

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:55.040
If you want to shoot me, go ahead.

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:56.040
However...

00:04:56.040 --> 00:05:00.050
...I would not commend you for wasting your ammunition.

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:03.380
Now that your purge orders have gone through formal channels,

00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:09.390
SO members Team 1 or 2 should be coming after us at any time.

00:05:09.390 --> 00:05:10.590
Depending on the circumstances,

00:05:10.590 --> 00:05:14.730
Internal Section 13 might also already have been brought into this.

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:17.060
Internal Section 13?

00:05:17.060 --> 00:05:22.300
Yes. GOTT's so-called "Purge Squad."

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:27.360
What's more, the prospects of our next dinner are nearly exhausted.

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:31.740
If you're serious about surviving, hadn't we better re-supply at once?

00:05:32.350 --> 00:05:33.970
I think so too.

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:42.690
If they think they can get clean away, I say let them try.

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:45.360
I do feel a bit bad for them, though.

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:46.990
There's no reason to.

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:51.190
I feel a lot worse for the bunch who gets sent out after them.

00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:00.710
This sure is some good Earl Grey.

00:06:00.710 --> 00:06:03.940
The aroma is moderate, without getting in the way.

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:07.050
Is something the matter?

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:11.310
It was something that I had been saving for those two.

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:16.390
The next time they came back, we had a date to enjoy it together.

00:06:16.390 --> 00:06:20.060
But as the days went by, the aroma began fading, you see...

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:23.530
"A broken broom brings an increase in litter."

00:06:23.530 --> 00:06:26.730
A tool is disposed of once its use has ended.

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:35.100
The next tool to be disposed of could possibly be myself.

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:44.220
Be extra careful not to miss anything in your inspection!

00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:47.150
The slightest misalignment could mean the difference between life and death!

00:06:50.690 --> 00:06:54.360
Attention all hands! The captain has something to say!

00:06:54.360 --> 00:07:00.700
The objectives of this operation are the two ES members, Éclair and Lumiere.

00:07:00.700 --> 00:07:01.840
However,

00:07:01.840 --> 00:07:06.370
the mission of this team is limited to controlling any dangerous elements.

00:07:06.370 --> 00:07:08.400
In other words, negotiation.

00:07:09.380 --> 00:07:15.080
Captain! Isn't this a case where the enforcement manual takes precedence?

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:20.720
I'm going to make sure that all of you return to Aineias.

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:26.730
I, as the squad captain, will take full responsibility. That is an order!

00:07:26.730 --> 00:07:31.400
Concentrate on securing the targets, and by no means take any hasty actions!

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:34.430
Now listen! The first rule of negotiation

00:07:34.430 --> 00:07:38.340
is always to arrive at a compromise through determined bargaining!

00:07:38.340 --> 00:07:40.670
Captain...

00:07:40.670 --> 00:07:45.780
Nobody has the right to destroy the life of a five-year-old boy.

00:07:45.780 --> 00:07:47.680
That's all there is to it.

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:50.310
He turns five next month.

00:07:51.690 --> 00:07:53.890
All hands, prepare to deploy for battle at once!

00:07:53.890 --> 00:07:56.320
We warp-out in three minutes!

00:08:04.360 --> 00:08:08.390
Yes, indeed... Well, food, at least...

00:08:12.370 --> 00:08:14.370
What did he mean by that?

00:08:14.370 --> 00:08:17.080
It would be too bad if he said more than that.

00:08:17.080 --> 00:08:20.670
He's only doing his job as an auditor.

00:08:24.380 --> 00:08:26.390
I'm sorry...

00:08:26.390 --> 00:08:31.060
I don't have any decent tea. Shall I prepare some wine for you?

00:08:31.060 --> 00:08:35.000
No, this is delicious. Thank you very much.

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:36.000
You're most kind.

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:39.670
Maybe, but I'm still upset about something.

00:08:39.670 --> 00:08:44.100
He's still at work, even while we're sitting here.

00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:46.670
We should be a little bit grateful to him.

00:08:46.670 --> 00:08:49.010
That may be true...

00:08:49.010 --> 00:08:52.880
We have to place the blame on the Nouvlesse.

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:55.020
Not on him, or the Chief.

00:08:55.020 --> 00:08:57.320
That much I know!

00:08:57.320 --> 00:09:00.680
But I just can't be so matter-of-fact about it, like you are!

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:09.860
Purged!? Those two!?

00:09:11.030 --> 00:09:15.430
You dummy, <i>Éc-chan.</i> This is because you're so coarse.

00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:20.940
Say, is the garlic on this pasta a little too strong?

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:25.710
They've landed at LAV-78.

00:09:25.710 --> 00:09:28.720
It's currently 1346 hours.

00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:31.380
Word should have reached there from the head office by now.

00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:33.650
Identification beacon cutoff!

00:09:33.650 --> 00:09:35.360
Begin approach to the general purpose docking

00:09:35.360 --> 00:09:37.990
on the northwest side of the standard bar.

00:09:37.990 --> 00:09:41.150
Approaching northwest general purpose docks.

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:43.660
Be that as it may,

00:09:43.660 --> 00:09:46.000
to get the purge order...

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:50.160
It's not just that. D command has been issued.

00:09:59.350 --> 00:10:02.680
The gentlemen from Internal Section 13, right?

00:10:02.680 --> 00:10:04.680
I'm afraid so.

00:10:04.680 --> 00:10:06.350
I should have known.

00:10:06.350 --> 00:10:09.690
Then that means they aren't letting us get away so easily?

00:10:09.690 --> 00:10:14.690
From a procedural standpoint, they have to confirm what your intentions are.

00:10:14.690 --> 00:10:15.700
Intentions?

00:10:15.700 --> 00:10:17.200
You could surrender,

00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:21.700
and ask whether you were right or wrong before a board of inquiry.

00:10:21.700 --> 00:10:24.700
In that case, my answer is "no."

00:10:24.700 --> 00:10:26.370
What about you?

00:10:26.370 --> 00:10:27.540
If you have been dispatched,

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:29.580
it means that even if we appeared before the board of inquiry,

00:10:29.580 --> 00:10:32.650
our chances of winning are slim.

00:10:32.650 --> 00:10:35.270
Is that so?

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:37.380
That's too bad.

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:07.080
Good luck.

00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:22.360
Why don't they get this started!?

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:25.090
They're probably using multiple tactics.

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:33.040
Internal Section 13 is an advance party, sent for containment.

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:37.380
The main unit, either Team 1 or 2, has probably been waiting for us to land.

00:11:37.380 --> 00:11:39.380
For an organization split up into so many divisions,

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:41.720
they sure do cooperate with each other at times like this!

00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:44.210
That just shows how serious they are!

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:48.050
Not her again...

00:11:48.050 --> 00:11:53.730
Even erasing her own memory herself, she still repeats the same life.

00:11:53.730 --> 00:11:57.800
Even if a thousand years were to go by, a waltz is still a waltz.

00:11:57.800 --> 00:11:59.990
The rhythm does not change.

00:12:03.400 --> 00:12:05.740
We're re-supplied, for the moment.

00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:09.080
We're taking off! Hurry!

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:13.080
Judging from your state, it would appear that they've reached even here.

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:16.380
You were correct! Hurry!

00:12:23.420 --> 00:12:24.650
Unleash them!

00:12:30.100 --> 00:12:32.000
Special weapons division, move forward!

00:12:39.040 --> 00:12:41.010
All hands, take aim!

00:12:43.380 --> 00:12:47.280
This is Lyall, of SO member Team 2!

00:12:48.050 --> 00:12:51.350
As of 1643 hours, on orders from the head office,

00:12:51.350 --> 00:12:54.050
we have taken measures to restrict your movement.

00:12:54.050 --> 00:12:56.590
Resistance will not do either one of us any good.

00:12:56.590 --> 00:12:59.060
We request that you surrender.

00:12:59.060 --> 00:13:00.730
And if we refuse?

00:13:00.730 --> 00:13:04.730
We will ask you once again. Surrender!

00:13:04.730 --> 00:13:06.600
We refuse.

00:13:12.070 --> 00:13:13.230
Start it up!

00:13:15.080 --> 00:13:18.810
Roger. Special weapons division, start it up!

00:13:22.080 --> 00:13:23.750
Are those?

00:13:23.750 --> 00:13:28.090
As you can see, those are no ordinary detaining wires.

00:13:28.090 --> 00:13:32.360
We have just set the triggering mechanisms at the joints.

00:13:32.360 --> 00:13:36.360
lf, by your resistance, those joints come apart,

00:13:36.360 --> 00:13:39.700
the biofuses inside will react and they will explode.

00:13:39.700 --> 00:13:43.370
Given the size of this colony, it will probably blow up half of it.

00:13:43.370 --> 00:13:47.040
That's ridiculous! If you do that, then you guys will also be...!

00:13:47.040 --> 00:13:51.340
Yes! That is exactly why we are asking you to surrender.

00:13:51.340 --> 00:13:55.710
Right now, you hold our lives in your hands!

00:14:04.390 --> 00:14:07.290
This is the last of the cuisine that we'll be eating here.

00:14:07.290 --> 00:14:09.020
Things will get hectic from here on.

00:14:10.730 --> 00:14:13.530
Do you suppose Éclair will beg for her life?

00:14:14.730 --> 00:14:15.930
That'll be the day.

00:14:17.070 --> 00:14:20.740
Right now, you are placing the lives of your subordinates in danger.

00:14:20.740 --> 00:14:22.080
That is correct.

00:14:22.080 --> 00:14:24.080
Not very fair, is it?

00:14:24.080 --> 00:14:27.100
Doesn't that go the same for you?

00:14:28.420 --> 00:14:30.420
You have become fugitives,

00:14:30.420 --> 00:14:34.690
and taken a Global Union auditor hostage.

00:14:34.690 --> 00:14:37.020
And there are other crimes, in addition.

00:14:37.020 --> 00:14:38.690
You don't mean!

00:14:38.690 --> 00:14:42.630
You tipped them off... as to where we were?

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:49.870
"Man is avarice; therefore is he man."

00:14:49.870 --> 00:14:52.390
Don't you think that is an interesting proverb?

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:59.050
If you want to shoot me, go ahead.

00:14:59.050 --> 00:15:03.450
However, I would not commend you for wasting your ammunition.

00:15:04.720 --> 00:15:06.390
Thanks to you, I have been rescued.

00:15:06.390 --> 00:15:09.150
Not at all. Well done.

00:15:13.060 --> 00:15:15.730
I don't want to let you die!

00:15:15.730 --> 00:15:18.700
And if we still say we refuse?

00:15:18.700 --> 00:15:23.070
We are well aware of how to survive under any circumstances.

00:15:23.070 --> 00:15:29.080
In that event, we would regrettably be forced to initiate D command!

00:15:29.080 --> 00:15:33.350
<i>Unless D command is initiated, there's no way for them to cope with us.</i>

00:15:33.350 --> 00:15:37.020
<i>However, will it be in time?</i>

00:15:37.020 --> 00:15:38.510
Surrender!

00:15:39.350 --> 00:15:42.080
Unfortunately, "No!"

00:15:49.700 --> 00:15:52.860
The detaining wires have been deactivated!

00:15:55.370 --> 00:15:58.570
Youssouf, initiate D command!

00:15:59.370 --> 00:16:01.710
That's not what you agreed to!

00:16:01.710 --> 00:16:05.040
Unfortunately, negotiations have broken down.

00:16:05.040 --> 00:16:06.380
But still...

00:16:06.380 --> 00:16:09.380
Youssouf, initiate D command!

00:16:09.380 --> 00:16:13.550
Roger! Special weapons division, initiate D command!

00:16:16.720 --> 00:16:19.730
Ignition, standby! Number, please!

00:16:19.730 --> 00:16:20.780
Stop this!

00:16:22.730 --> 00:16:28.130
2-3-6-2-0-6-7-9!

00:16:29.400 --> 00:16:31.230
Initiating D command!

00:16:52.030 --> 00:16:56.000
D command is a transmission that forces the nanocells,

00:16:56.000 --> 00:17:00.370
or nanomachines, inside them to expand.

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:03.700
L- Lu... mi... ere!

00:17:03.700 --> 00:17:06.140
Éc... lair!

00:17:07.370 --> 00:17:11.540
The expanded cells apply pressure to the organs,

00:17:11.540 --> 00:17:13.710
which are soon destroyed.

00:17:13.710 --> 00:17:17.380
I know that! So why did you initiate it!?

00:17:17.380 --> 00:17:20.350
Because it is our job to do so!

00:17:20.350 --> 00:17:24.720
In order to defend the organization, somebody has to do this...

00:17:24.720 --> 00:17:28.660
...this so-called dirty work! Thanks to us,

00:17:28.660 --> 00:17:33.600
our families are able to safely reach their birthdays every year!

00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:42.640
<i>Antimist... vaccine! I have to make them act... as antibodies!</i>

00:17:53.690 --> 00:17:56.310
<i>Éclair, too...</i>

00:18:02.700 --> 00:18:05.860
It's no use! I'm not going to make it in time!

00:18:09.700 --> 00:18:11.640
Please do not move!

00:18:13.370 --> 00:18:15.380
What are you doing!?

00:18:15.380 --> 00:18:18.310
No matter how long a lifetime one may wish to lead,

00:18:18.310 --> 00:18:21.050
these girls are still young.

00:18:21.050 --> 00:18:25.880
Nobody has the right to destroy the future these girls have.

00:18:28.390 --> 00:18:32.520
The Global Union's... ES members!

00:18:55.010 --> 00:18:58.020
Get her the antibodies right away.

00:18:58.020 --> 00:19:00.690
I have stopped time for her briefly.

00:19:00.690 --> 00:19:05.690
I think that all of her memories will probably return as a result of this.

00:19:05.690 --> 00:19:08.030
It may be cruel...

00:19:08.030 --> 00:19:12.370
...but it is better than dying, isn't it?

00:19:12.370 --> 00:19:16.340
Everyone dreams of becoming immortally young.

00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:20.400
The problem is how one comes to live with it.

00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:41.330
Éclair, I'm giving you antibodies now...

00:19:41.330 --> 00:19:45.160
"Man is avarice; therefore is he man."

00:19:45.160 --> 00:19:48.670
In other words, don't overdo it.

00:19:48.670 --> 00:19:51.000
What do you mean?

00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:56.110
It's simple. You should accept things the way they are.

00:19:56.110 --> 00:19:59.680
Including the life ahead of you. Including the future ahead of you.

00:19:59.680 --> 00:20:03.020
What you say is difficult.

00:20:03.020 --> 00:20:10.020
Knowing you, you'll be all right. Otherwise, I wouldn't have helped you.

00:20:10.020 --> 00:20:11.360
Then...

00:20:11.360 --> 00:20:15.700
They say that to deceive your enemies, begin with their friends, don't they?

00:20:15.700 --> 00:20:17.700
Thanks.

00:20:17.700 --> 00:20:20.500
However, unfortunately,

00:20:20.500 --> 00:20:24.370
I think it would be better if I am not with you any longer.

00:20:24.370 --> 00:20:27.370
I am, after all an auditor.

00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:31.640
That's okay. I've said a lot of terrible things to you.

00:20:31.640 --> 00:20:34.880
Hey, it's nothing I couldn't take.

00:20:39.320 --> 00:20:45.220
Is this... the auditor's? No, it's the girl's power!

00:20:45.220 --> 00:20:47.330
It's nearly G-class!

00:20:47.330 --> 00:20:51.920
She's over spec! She's not the sort of opponent that we can handle!

00:21:01.670 --> 00:21:04.770
The two appear to have escaped.

00:21:09.350 --> 00:21:13.380
1749 hours. Target has been lost.

00:21:14.690 --> 00:21:17.120
We're going to withdraw now!

00:21:32.040 --> 00:21:32.900
Good luck!

00:23:07.020 --> 00:23:11.020
<i>There are threads that we call destiny
that tie one person to another.</i>

00:23:11.020 --> 00:23:14.120
<i>Does the hand that is extended clasp another?</i>

00:23:14.120 --> 00:23:16.030
<i>Or does it strike another?</i>

00:23:16.030 --> 00:23:20.260
<i>Next time on Kiddy Grade</i>
